                "To resolve this procyclical vulnerability, the International Accounting Standards Board (IASB) and the Institute of Chartered Accountants of India (ICAI) promulgated the revolutionary Expected Credit Loss (ECL) standard, codified under IFRS 9 and Ind AS 109 (Financial Instruments). The ECL framework abandons the backward-looking incurred loss trigger in favor of a dynamic, forward-looking staging model that mandates continuous, probabilistic estimation of credit impairment from the exact day a loan is originated. Under Ind AS 109, all financial assets measured at amortized cost or fair value through other comprehensive income (FVOCI) are categorized into one of three sequential stages reflecting their credit migration trajectory.",
