                "A critical empirical challenge in implementing the Merton model is that the total asset value VA and asset volatility sigma_A are unobservable directly, because only equity E is publicly traded on stock exchanges. Merton resolved this by formulating a system of two simultaneous non-linear equations utilizing Ito's Lemma: (1) the Black-Scholes equity call equation; and (2) the equity volatility relationship linking observable equity volatility sigma_E with unobservable asset volatility sigma_A: sigma_E = (VA / E) * N(d1) * sigma_A. By solving this bivariate system numerically, risk analysts back out the unobservable market value of assets VA and the underlying asset volatility sigma_A.",
